<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The warmth button in the compact controls: a sun on the horizon, which is what "warmth" looks
    like without borrowing the icon that means the other mechanism. A plain sun means *brightness* —
    Android's word for the backlight (CONTEXT.md) — and putting one on this button would name the
    thing Gloam is most often mistaken for.

    Hand-drawn for the same reason ic_timer is: this project depends on material-icons-core only
    (gradle/libs.versions.toml), which has no twilight glyph in it. Strokes rather than a filled
    silhouette, so the geometry is checkable: a horizon at y=20, the ground line the dome sits on at
    y=16, a half-disc of radius 6 above it, and three rays. Compose's `Icon` tints the painter, so
    the colours here only have to be opaque.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24">
